# `S-2a` — the page's round trip, written the way a newcomer would (review decision 15): a new file
# on the API door, a request composed by the dialog, `send` to see what comes back, a value ticked
# into an assertion, the file written, `⌘↩` to run it, and the report read on the Run tab. Needs the
# stack: the request is the dogfood API's `/health`, sent from the scratch copy's config.
#
# **After tflw `M241`** this file gains an action and a crawl — the two declarations the page cannot
# author yet.

test "a file written on the API door is sent, asserted, run and read back"
  let token = env(TFLW_UI_TOKEN)
  open "/?token={token}#/api"
  click css "[data-compose-new-file]"
  fill field "file path" with "tests/api/written-in-the-page.tflw"
  fill field "test name" with "the health check answers, in a file the page wrote"
  fill field "request path" with "/health"
  click css "[data-new-create]"
  expect css "[data-new-thing]" has count 0
  within css "[data-files]"
    expect text "written-in-the-page.tflw" is visible
  click css "[data-seq-row=request] [data-seq-pick]"
  click css "[data-compose-send=this]"
  expect css "[data-compose-response=\"200\"]" is visible
  click css "[data-compose-response]"
  tick css "[data-tick=db]"
  click css "[data-compose-verify]"
  click css "[data-compose-write]"
  expect css "[data-compose-dirty]" has count 0
  press "Control+Enter"
  click css "[data-tab=run]"
  expect text "the health check answers, in a file the page wrote" is visible
